@startuml
!include _style.puml
title Payment and OrderGroup Payment Status
hide empty description
state "Payment: PENDING\nOrderGroup: PENDING" as Pending
state "Payment: SUCCESS\nOrderGroup: PAID" as Paid
state "Payment: FAILED\nOrderGroup: FAILED" as Failed
state "Payment: PARTIALLY_REFUNDED\nOrderGroup: PARTIALLY_REFUNDED" as Partial
state "Payment: REFUNDED\nOrderGroup: REFUNDED" as Refunded
state "Payment: PENDING\nOrderGroup: FAILED\n(all unpaid orders cancelled)" as CancelledUnpaid

[*] --> Pending : OrderDraftFactory.create()\nno gateway transaction ID yet
Pending --> Pending : initiatePayment() / GW-TXN-UUID\nor restart existing nonprocessed payment
Pending --> Paid : successful callback/simulation\nor internal orchestration success
Pending --> Failed : unsuccessful callback/simulation\nor internal orchestration failure
Failed --> Pending : initiatePayment()\n[valid positive total and method]
Failed --> Paid : PaymentService successful callback\n[transaction unchanged; not refunded]
Failed --> Failed : failed callback\nor duplicate orchestration failure
Paid --> Paid : repeated successful callback / no-op
Paid --> Partial : processPartialRefund()\n[0 < accumulated refund < payment.amount]
Partial --> Partial : processPartialRefund()\n[accumulated refund < payment.amount]
Paid --> Refunded : partial refund reaches full amount\nor processFullRefund()
Partial --> Refunded : remaining amount refunded
Pending --> CancelledUnpaid : customerCancelOrder()\n[all unpaid sub-orders CANCELLED]
CancelledUnpaid --> Pending : direct initiatePayment()\n[no sub-order-state check]
CancelledUnpaid --> Paid : direct successful callback\n[cancelled sub-orders remain cancelled]
CancelledUnpaid --> Failed : direct failed callback

note right of Partial
Partial refunds require SUCCESS/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED,
positive amount <= order total and remaining payment balance,
and a nonblank reason. They set the target Order=CANCELLED.
Full refund refunds the remaining amount and cancels
non-COMPLETED sub-orders. Refunds are bookkeeping,
without an external payment gateway integration.
SubOrderService also derives group refund status from
cancelled order counts; it can differ from monetary status
if direct Admin partial refunds use arbitrary amounts.
end note
note left of Failed
PaymentService failure sets Payment/Group=FAILED only.
Orchestration failure requires pending group/payment/orders,
releases stock and cancels all sub-orders.
Orchestration success has the same pending guards and publishes
OrderPaidEvent; PaymentService sends notifications directly.
end note
note right of Refunded
initiatePayment rejects SUCCESS and refunded states.
Callbacks reject refunded states and attempts to fail SUCCESS.
Frontend payment proxy requires all sub-orders pending
and both group and payment PENDING before simulation.
Group-only cancellation does not change Payment status.
end note
